  "decision": "As KerML 8.2.5.12 states it: `#` followed by one PrefixMetadataFeature, which the same clause defines as an OwnedFeatureTyping, so in practice `#` and a type name. This is the KerML variant (ADR-0014). SysML states the production with a PrefixMetadataUsage in place of the PrefixMetadataFeature, and that difference is why the production is split. The clause prints the PrefixMetadataFeature production with `:` where `=` belongs. That defect is in PrefixMetadataFeature's own text, not here, and its own unit should record it. The Xtext rule agrees.",
